From: Linghao Zhang <linghao.zhang@kemaro.ch>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 16:08:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] torizon: set boot_conf instead of appending to it

board_late_init() of the Adlink board-support patch builds boot_conf as
"<current boot_conf>#<SKU overlay>" on every boot (a fresh environment even
yields a literal "<NULL>" prefix). Torizon's update rollback counter saves the
whole environment after an OTA install, so the value persists and grows by one
entry per update boot. It stops growing once the command no longer fits the
256-byte buffer the vendor code formats it into; from then on setenv fails
with a syntax error on every boot and boot_conf keeps its stored value.

U-Boot derives the SKU overlay from the hardware pins at every boot, so the
old value is never needed: set boot_conf to exactly that overlay.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Linghao Zhang <linghao.zhang@kemaro.ch>
---
 board/mediatek/lec_mtk_i1200/lec_mtk_i1200.c | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/board/mediatek/lec_mtk_i1200/lec_mtk_i1200.c b/board/mediatek/lec_mtk_i1200/lec_mtk_i1200.c
--- a/board/mediatek/lec_mtk_i1200/lec_mtk_i1200.c
+++ b/board/mediatek/lec_mtk_i1200/lec_mtk_i1200.c
@@ -297,7 +297,6 @@ static void reset_ethphy(void)
 
 int board_late_init(void)
 {
-	char *boot_conf_orig = env_get("boot_conf");
 	char cmd[256];
 
     uint32_t sku_id_0 = (*(volatile uint32_t *)SKU_REG >> SKU_BIT0) & 0x1;
@@ -312,7 +311,7 @@ int board_late_init(void)
     for (i = 0; i < sizeof(skus)/sizeof(struct sku_info); i++) {
         if (skus[i].sku_id == sku_id) {
 		printf("SKU:   %s\n", skus[i].sku_str);
-		snprintf(cmd, sizeof(cmd), "setenv boot_conf '%s#%s'", boot_conf_orig, skus[i].dtbo_file);
+		snprintf(cmd, sizeof(cmd), "setenv boot_conf '%s'", skus[i].dtbo_file);
 		run_command(cmd, 0);
 		break;
         }
